  &lt;body>
    &lt;p>
&lt;b>The additional anonymous unions to assert the disjointness of temporary situations in UML as per &lt;a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nemo-ufes/gufo/master/gufo.ttl">gufo.ttl       
&lt;/a>&lt;/b>&lt;br>Due to a tool limitation, additional anonymous unions must be used to assert the disjointness of temporary situations as defined by gufo.ttl (shown here as «Disjoint» dependencies created by CCM on import). The two anonymous «Union» classes have been added manually.

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
      
&lt;br>The issue is due to &lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1700503998866_696161_5204" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="AUTOMATIC_UPDATE">TemporaryConstitutionSituation&lt;/a> not being disjoint with &lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1700503998816_727633_5073" erit:display="CUSTOM_TEXT" erit:update="NO_UPDATE">TemporaryParthoodSituation&lt;/a>. It may be that this is an error in the TTL file and in fact all the temporary situation classes should be pairwise disjoint, but it is not clear from comparing the definitions in the «Literal Annotation» notes for these two classes that they are in fact disjoint. In order to create generalization sets in UML that express the relevant disjointness, two anonymous «Union» classes are needed. This is due to the tool correctly interpreting multiple instances of a generalization between two classes as being exactly the same relationship, which it enforces as a automatic rule that prevents the same generalization belong to more than one generalization set      
&lt;br>

    &lt;/p>

&lt;/body>
